<comment datatype='string'>Among 13 &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-321846&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Pseudomonas simiae&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt; genes that were found to be consistently important for utilization of &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?type=COMPOUND&amp;object=2-DEOXYRIBOSE&quot; title=&quot;&lt;a href=''/META/NEW-IMAGE?type=COMPOUND&amp;object=2-DEOXYRIBOSE''&gt;2-deoxy-D-ribose&lt;/a&gt; has many different forms in solution inclding &lt;a href=''/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-22231''&gt;2-deoxy-&amp;beta;-D-ribopyranose&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=''/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-22232''&gt;2-deoxy-&amp;alpha;-D-ribopyranose&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=''/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-22287''&gt;2-deoxy-&amp;beta;-D-ribofuranose&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=''/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-22286''&gt;2-deoxy-&amp;alpha;-D-ribofuranose&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=''/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-22284''&gt;open chain&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;The open-chain structure shown here is provided only as a schematic illustration of chirality. Consult the appropriate class instances for information on specific ring structures and their anomeric configuration.&quot;&gt;2-deoxy-D-ribose&lt;/a&gt; and were not important for fitness under most other conditions was a gene encoding an enzyme similar to &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?type=EC-NUMBER&amp;object=EC-2.3.1.9&quot;&gt;EC 2.3.1.9, acetyl-CoA &lt;em&gt;C&lt;/em&gt;-acetyltransferase&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
A mutant with a mutation in this gene could grow on glucose, but was not able to grow on either &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?type=COMPOUND&amp;object=2-DEOXYRIBOSE&quot; title=&quot;&lt;a href=''/META/NEW-IMAGE?type=COMPOUND&amp;object=2-DEOXYRIBOSE''&gt;2-deoxy-D-ribose&lt;/a&gt; has many different forms in solution inclding &lt;a href=''/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-22231''&gt;2-deoxy-&amp;beta;-D-ribopyranose&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=''/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-22232''&gt;2-deoxy-&amp;alpha;-D-ribopyranose&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=''/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-22287''&gt;2-deoxy-&amp;beta;-D-ribofuranose&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=''/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-22286''&gt;2-deoxy-&amp;alpha;-D-ribofuranose&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=''/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-22284''&gt;open chain&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;The open-chain structure shown here is provided only as a schematic illustration of chirality. Consult the appropriate class instances for information on specific ring structures and their anomeric configuration.&quot;&gt;2-deoxy-D-ribose&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-16715&quot;&gt;2-deoxy-D-ribonate&lt;/a&gt;, indicating that the enzyme is involved in the &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?type=PATHWAY&amp;object=PWY-8058&quot;&gt;2-deoxy-D-ribose degradation II&lt;/a&gt; pathway [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/30746495&quot;&gt;Price19&lt;/a&gt;].</comment>
